Z||000000||V8Fiero||06-25-2001||11:34 PM||||Ok, I just got back last Tuesday from going to WV to pick up an 86 GT with a seized engine from the Fiero Warehouse. I got an extra running engine with the car. I started the swap on Friday afternoon. Worked from 10:30 am on Sat. to 10:00 pm. Had the good engine on the cradle, switched wiring harness, and the tranny with the engine as well. By the end of Sat. the engine was back underneath the car ready to bolt the cradle up. Sun just bolted the cradle back in and started to put the suspension back together. Just got too dang hot. <P>Tonight I finished the suspension, new brakes, filled all the fluids, finished hooking up the computer, and installed the battery. Went to fire it up.........................................................................................and.............IT FIRED UP IN 2 SECS!!!!!<P>I was so excited. This is my first GT. Had to give it a bath right away......Im still excited that I can hardly stand it!!!! Still have to "burp" the cooling system and make sure there are now leaks. Looks good so far.....<P>Thanks again Doug.<BR>Now I just have to install the new sail panels...<P>Sorry so long...just wanted to share my JOY<P>Scott||||reg||14
